WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.685
What a working engineer would do.

2
00:00:01.965 --> 00:00:16.216
Build the dataset with a script, never by hand in a spreadsheet, so every step is repeatable and reviewable: validate, quarantine, deduplicate, split with groups and strata, check leakage, freeze the test set, write a manifest.

3
00:00:16.496 --> 00:00:22.981
Run it in CI when the data changes, the same way Studio 3 gated prompt changes on evals.

4
00:00:23.261 --> 00:00:31.347
Read samples at every stage: the pairs near your near-duplicate threshold, the quarantined labels, a random handful of each split.

5
00:00:31.627 --> 00:00:41.973
And keep two habits that protect the score: iterate on validation, report on test, and refresh the test set from production on a schedule instead of polishing the old one.

6
00:00:42.253 --> 00:00:49.485
The lab puts all of this together for the action-item task, and its output is in the format next week’s training tools accept.
